From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:13:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] yblod-57: make the Dolby Vision diagnostics cheap when
 nobody reads them

DVBRIDGE::RenderUsage opened and parsed every /proc/self/fdinfo entry
(up to 512) per sample: every 500 ms on the GUI thread while the player
information panel is open, and every 10 s on the video thread during
Dolby Vision playback, whose "DVBridge playback health" line went to the
log at INFO in every playback, since an unset DVBRIDGE_DIAGNOSTICS means
on.

- RenderUsage remembers which descriptors are DRM files and opens only
  those (and new descriptors); the list is forgotten every 30 s, as a
  descriptor number can be reused.
- The health line is written at INFO only with DVBRIDGE_DIAGNOSTICS=1,
  at DEBUG otherwise, and is not sampled at all unless one of the two
  would show it. The bounded failure reports DVBRIDGE_DIAGNOSTICS also
  governs are unchanged.
- RenderUsage's code moves from the header to DVRenderUsage.cpp, so
  its includers no longer pull in <filesystem>, <fstream> and
  <sstream>.
